From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: restore kaanapali DP0 registration and the idle guard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backport the accepted Kaanapali DP0 changes to this 7.2.6 DP display
driver.  The vendor DP controller 0 lives at 0x09ad2000 (dp_ahb
0x9ad2000, dp_aux +0x200, dp_link 0x9ad3000, dp_p0 0x9ad4000), wide
bus like sm8650, compatible "qcom,kaanapali-dp".  Without the
descriptor the DP platform device stays unbound and the DPU aggregate
never completes its components.

The original change also skipped PUSH_IDLE from
msm_dp_bridge_atomic_disable() when the display never came up.  The
7.3 rebase dropped that hunk because upstream had since fixed the same
problem, but this 7.2.6 source still calls msm_dp_ctrl_push_idle()
unconditionally.  Restore the guard here: when link training fails,
msm_dp_ctrl_deinitialize_mainlink() has already turned the link clocks
and the PHY off with power_on still false, so writing
REG_DP_STATE_CTRL then is an unclocked access (900E dump mode on
TB323FU).  The clock-off callbacks and all other behavior stay
unchanged.

The DP0 descriptor and compatible table entries are copied from the
accepted TB323FU 0051 patch and remain Joonhoe Kim's work; the guard is
restored in the form that series carried before its 7.3 rebase.  No new
hardware or network verification is claimed by this backport.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -104,6 +104,11 @@ static const struct msm_dp_desc msm_dp_desc_glymur[] = {
 	{}
 };
 
+static const struct msm_dp_desc msm_dp_desc_kaanapali[] = {
+	{ .io_start = 0x09ad2000, .id = MSM_DP_CONTROLLER_0, .wide_bus_supported = true },
+	{}
+};
+
 static const struct msm_dp_desc msm_dp_desc_sa8775p[] = {
 	{ .io_start = 0x0af54000, .id = MSM_DP_CONTROLLER_0, .wide_bus_supported = true },
 	{ .io_start = 0x0af5c000, .id = MSM_DP_CONTROLLER_1, .wide_bus_supported = true },
@@ -162,6 +167,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id msm_dp_dt_match[] = {
 
 static const struct of_device_id msm_dp_dt_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-dp", .data = &msm_dp_desc_glymur },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,kaanapali-dp", .data = &msm_dp_desc_kaanapali },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sa8775p-dp", .data = &msm_dp_desc_sa8775p },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc7180-dp", .data = &msm_dp_desc_sc7180 },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc7280-dp", .data = &msm_dp_desc_sc7280 },
@@ -1412,7 +1418,8 @@ void msm_dp_bridge_atomic_disable(struct drm_bridge *drm_bridge,
 
 	msm_dp_display = container_of(dp, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 
-	msm_dp_ctrl_push_idle(msm_dp_display->ctrl);
+	if (dp->power_on)
+		msm_dp_ctrl_push_idle(msm_dp_display->ctrl);
 }
 
 void msm_dp_bridge_atomic_post_disable(struct drm_bridge *drm_bridge,
